# Agent contract and dev process (all agents)

Both files are hash-versioned and are injected automatically into every COMPILED dispatch. If you are
working from an ad-hoc chat rather than a compiled dispatch, nothing injected them for you — read them
yourself before substantive work:

- `90_runbooks/AGENT_CONTRACT.md` — the lane-planner fan model (you may spawn sub-agents; you supervise
  every one to completion, you never delegate verification below yourself, you adversarially review
  every deliverable, and you file CP1/CP2 checkpoints), interruption recovery, the one-bulk-writer-slot
  law, heavy-scan serialization, the verification rules, and the machine-checkable close schema.
- `90_runbooks/DEV_PROCESS.md` — how work is shaped and judged. A coverage figure travels with its
  denominator. Classes are measured, never derived by subtraction. An instrument's exclusion set is part
  of its contract. A gating indicator is proven able to FIRE before it is trusted. Paired controls need a
  divergence test. A guardrail that does not survive a clone is not a guardrail.

`AGENTS.md` at the repo root is the full reading order for any tool.

**No dispatch without a plan row.** Dispatches are compiled with `node scripts/dispatch.mjs`, never
hand-assembled; the canon-gate hook blocks anything missing the markers.
